WEBVTT
Kind: captions

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.510 position:63% line:0%
This is how we’re getting to the moon.

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:06.480 position:63% line:0%
NASA’s SLS lifts the Orion spacecraft carrying
astronauts.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.170 position:63% line:0%
Orion meets up with a lunar variant of Starship
in lunar orbit.

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:15.879 position:63% line:0%
The crew transfers to Starship, which takes
them to the moon's surface.

00:00:15.879 --> 00:00:21.050 position:63% line:0%
For the trip home, Starship lifts off, meets
up with Orion, which was left in lunar orbit,

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:24.570 position:63% line:0%
the crew transfers over to Orion, and returns
to Earth.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:29.849 position:63% line:0%
But what if…Starship was used to go all
the way from earth to the moon?

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:34.560 position:63% line:0%
Starship could launch, meet up with another
Starship to refuel, before journeying to the

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.570 position:63% line:0%
moon.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:39.570 position:63% line:0%
This version of Starship is not the lunar
variant.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:43.239 position:63% line:0%
It requires the heat shield and flaps for
landing back on earth.

